# brace-expansion DoS (GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr / GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7 /
# GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p) was bundled inside aws-cdk-lib's minimatch dependency and
# could not be fixed via package.json overrides, since npm overrides do not apply
# to bundled dependencies. RESOLVED as of aws-cdk-lib 2.273.0, which bundles
# brace-expansion 5.0.12 (above the vulnerable <= 5.0.11 range) via minimatch
# 10.2.5. `npm audit --omit=dev` is now clean (0 vulnerabilities).
#
# The remaining `npm audit` findings are a dev-only Jest coverage chain
# (sprintf-js GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c -> argparse@1 -> js-yaml@3 ->
# @istanbuljs/load-nyc-config -> babel-plugin-istanbul -> @jest/*). They are
# moderate, absent from `--omit=dev`, and have no clean upstream fix:
# @istanbuljs/load-nyc-config still pins the old js-yaml/argparse chain, and
# `npm audit fix --force` would downgrade ts-jest (a breaking change) without
# resolving them. Intentionally not force-fixed. Re-check on every aws-cdk-lib
# upgrade.
audit-level=critical
